l":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39864165984/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39864165984/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39864165984/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/workflows/365585056","head_commit":{"id":"69310bf79fb5dff0151438d26a6ca6763b749d1c","tree_id":"d29d05208acc270af78fe3a522b48523e74805b5","message":"T-3036: Glessner's stable cupola's corners meet without dark strips (#1217)\n\ndovecote_band built each of the cupola body's four faces as a 0.08 m slab\nrunning the plan's full width, so every slab's end cap lay in its\nneighbour's front face at the corner (coplanar), and solid_polygon left\neach edge face to the polygon's winding, which the plane's axis and sign\nmirror: on the west and north faces (x0, y1) the caps looked inward. The\neast and west walls now take the corners and the north and south walls\nbutt inside them, and a local outward_solid turns every edge face of the\nwalls and landing ledges out of the solid. Probe over the band's faces:\n20 inward-facing faces and 58 overlapping coplanar pairs in the outer\nplanes before, 0 and 0 after. No dimension moved.\n\nRebaked glessner_house (masters, web derivatives, light tier, archive\nrepacked); HABS 01, the Cornell view and HABS 15 re-rendered and their\nmatch records reviewed: the strips are gone from both northwest views.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward <steward@polecat.live>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:19:59Z","author":{"name":"Kevin Haas","email":"kevinroberthaas@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com"}},"repository":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","private":false,"owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","a