ttps://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/check-suites/107947324681","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39828177249/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39828177249/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39828177249/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/workflows/365585056","head_commit":{"id":"cdee9c69851f5585249809c05188915c0fd942a6","tree_id":"ff795d8690b94d966163958cadaf55476042250b","message":"T-3030: Glessner's stable hoist stone as its 4 ft cantilever, cupola ledges wrapped (#1204)\n\nThe c. 1887 Cornell view sees the hoist stone's west side face from the\nnorthwest: through its solved camera (local offset at the arch's crown\nremoved) the side runs 62 px from wall to nose, which a 4.0 ft projection\ngives (1.75 ft gives 27). Its end face reads 0.75 ft wide and 0.83 ft deep.\nHABS 01 puts the nose where a 3-4 ft projection does; its long dark band\nalong the wall is the stone's cast shadow, not a beam. HABS 15 sees the lit\nsloping underside (about 42 px, a 3.6 ft projection) and the foot about\n10 px lower. So: W 140.75-141.5, foot 26.0 ft, top 28.15 ft, 4.0 ft out,\n0.83 ft nose (new optional `nose_ft`). Both northwest prints run the\ncupola's landing ledges unbroken round its corners; they now wrap\n(`ledge_corners: wrapped`, opt-in, no other building changes).\n\nRebaked glessner_house (archive repacked, K01 baseline re-measured,\nsource-use coverage rebuilt); the three stable-end match records reviewed\nand kept `differs` with what stays open. The cupola's height is split out\nas T-3031 (Cornell and HABS 01 disagree on it). L-glessner-hoist-3030.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward <steward@polecat.live>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:04:20Z","author":{"name":"Kevin Haas","email":"kevinroberthaas@